# Site context — the portfolio the guestbook lives in

Justin Poli's portfolio site, built with the Astryx design system. Production is live at justinpoli.is-a.dev (commit 46d6a34, shipped 2026-11-05 ~7:53 PM EST). This file is the context a builder needs; every claim here is quoted from `spec/astryx/DESIGN.md` or the code, not from memory.

## Concept

One WebGL field of 6,144 lanes (one per CUDA core of the RTX 3070 Ti), one draw call. The field morphs between scenes by changing four uniform weights. Routes:

- `/` server: lanes parallel, warps of 32, stack words drift out left.
- `/leaflink`: ink streets on paper, mutual aid, never "event discovery".
- `/sidequests`: chalk campus plan on blueprint blue, 3 quest trails.

Only nav is the bottom-edge keymap (1 server, 2 leaflink, 3 sidequests, w whoami, c contact) as real `<a href>` links. Document height equals viewport height at every route. `window.__lanefield.laneCount === 6144` everywhere.

## The field is 3D

Lanes have x/y/z positions. The camera has a position, target, and field of view (`src/world/camera.ts`, `src/world/layouts/server.ts`). The coarse server camera (DESIGN 1.4.0, shipped 2026-11-05): pos [-3.5, 5.0, 12.0], target [0.3, 0.0, -3.0], fovDeg 52, shiftNdc [0.0, -0.3], pitch -17.91. The fine (desktop) server camera is unchanged. The SideQuests camera band is pitchMin -75 / pitchMax -5 (enforced by clampSideQuestsPitch on the SideQuests path only). There is no server camera band.

## Spec and copy

- `spec/astryx/DESIGN.md` is the design spec (section 12 token block is authoritative; section 6.13 is GLITTERBOX). New design values go into DESIGN.md first (version bump + dated changelog) before code.
- `spec/astryx/specs/S09-copy-deck.md` (v1.5.0) is the copy source of truth. `src/copy.ts` is generated by `tools/extract-copy.mjs`, never hand-edit. `src/tokens.generated.ts` is generated by `tools/extract-tokens.mjs`.
- Landing copy (S09 1.4.0, Justin-approved): P1 "Computer science senior at SUNY New Paltz. I like to build my own tools." P2 "LeafLink and SideQuests both took 2nd place at their hackathons, and I run my own LLM inference server at home." Sekiro stays in the whoami sheet: "Favorite game: Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice."
- SideQuests copy (S09 1.5.0, Justin-approved): C-SQ-P1 "A community platform anyone can host, built as quests on ActivityPub. Each community runs its own instance and sets its own quests."
- Meta description: "Justin Poli. Computer science senior at SUNY New Paltz, graduating December 2027. Runs his own LLM inference server at home."
- Agent-readability files (llms.txt, llms-full.txt, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, JSON-LD Person, OG/Twitter meta) must match the human-visible site on every fact. No hidden text. No phone number ever on the site.

## Tokens

Void ground #0A0C0F, raised #15171B, text #E6E8EA, text2 #A7ABB0, accent #7BB5F8, hairline #E6E8EA21. Paper ground #F3F0EA, text #14161A, accent #0E3565. Field ground #10294E, text #F5F1E9, accent #7BB5F8. Signal #7BB5F8, signalDim #4F77A5, signalHot #D4E7FC, ink #0E3565, chalk #F5F1E9. Type: Commit Mono only. Travel 700ms, wordCadence 1600ms.

## Motion the site already has

- Morphs between 3D scene layouts (server, leaflink, sidequests, scatter).
- Bulge/ripple effects on LeafLink and SideQuests.
- Stochastic/randomized game-style motion (Justin's preference: unique every time, entropy/parallax, morphs flush, a seamless shape-shifter transformation).
- Camera tracking on mobile.
- GLITTERBOX (DESIGN 6.13, `src/chrome/glitterbox.ts`): press and hold anywhere on the lane field (or hold the `g` key) and the lanes come apart into glitter around the touch, swirling with a seeded direction; let go and they re-form. No tab, no page, no copy, no new asset. It is a mode of the one material the site is made of. GLITTERBOX is NOT used in the guestbook (axed 2026-11-09).

## Brand rules (DESIGN.md sections 9/10)

No photos, no illustrations, no icons except the built-in external-link indicator, no third-party logos, all visuals procedural. Exactly one data-brand-mark each on LeafLink (logo.png from bon3head/LeafLink) and SideQuests (sidequests.gif from opensourcery/sidequests; sidequests-alpha.gif is DO NOT USE), max 12% of viewport; none on server or whoami.

## Budgets

LCP 2000ms, TTI 3000, TBT 150, CLS 0.02, appShellJsGz 110 KB (at last measurement 145.27 KB, over budget, follow-up open, budget unchanged), worldChunkGz 220 KB (at last measurement 209.71 KB), drawCallsMax 12, gpuMemoryMbMax 64. Gate command: `npm run gates`. Read gate exit codes directly, never through a pipe. Gates never lowered; budget/threshold changes only via a DESIGN.md patch with the measurement in the changelog.

## Repo and deployment

- Repo: https://github.com/bon3head/PersonalSite. Branches: astryx-polish-r2 (development), astryx-integration (preview), main (stale at 14ab8df). Never merge draft PR bon3head/PersonalSite#1.
- Vercel: project justin-poli-astryx (prj_XNS96fctj2Id4d6Qxi1zZNkjaYrY), team "Justin's projects". Production is done by `create_deployment` redeploy with `target: "production"` (request_promote returns 422 on this project). Custom domain justinpoli.is-a.dev (live, verified).
- Banned-scan quirk: `node tools/banned-scan.mjs dist` (no trailing slash) exits 0 clean; with trailing slash it false-flags library code.

## Naming

Astryx is Meta's design system and tooling, the baseline the site is built on. Never call the site, the portfolio, or the mark "Astryx". The mark is Justin Poli's portfolio reasoning mark, built with the Astryx design system.
</file>

